// Jest Snapshot v1, https://goo.gl/fbAQLP

exports[`schemaDoc lists the modules and mechanic kinds with no query 1`] = `
"# Spec modules

Top-level keys of a spec. Look one up with \`chaincraft docs schema <module>\`.

| Module | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \`metadata\` | yes | Game title, player count, and randomness configuration. |
| \`players\` | no | Role definitions, assignment rules, and player-scoped properties. |
| \`gamepieceTypes\` | no | Gamepiece type definitions — properties, inventory slots, and action slots. |
| \`inventories\` | no | Inventory type declarations — structure, scope, capacity, and visibility. |
| \`state\` | no | Abstract state declarations — game and per-player properties with no physical gamepiece representation. |
| \`effects\` | no | Named reusable effects — referenced by actions and flow hooks. |
| \`actions\` | no | Player-facing actions — inputs, preconditions, and effect sequences. |
| \`flow\` | yes | Game structural skeleton — loop/turn/simultaneous nodes, hooks, and interrupts. |
| \`catalog\` | no | Piece registry — declares what pieces exist and their initial property values. |
| \`mechanics\` | no | Game-level mechanic declarations (score tracks, dominant-gamepiece evaluation, etc.). |

# Mechanic kinds

Look one up with \`chaincraft docs schema <kind>\`.

## GameMechanic

| \`kind\` | Description |
|---|---|
| \`chaincraft:score-track\` | Game-level mechanic: tracks player or team scores on a line-structure board. |
| \`chaincraft:dominant-gamepiece\` | Game-level mechanic: ranks gamepieces in an inventory via a chain of comparison rules and resolves an overall winner. |

## PieceMechanic

| \`kind\` | Description |
|---|---|
| \`chaincraft:charges\` | Piece-scoped mechanic: gates an action behind a charge cost drawn from a piece's own inventory. |
| \`chaincraft:conversion\` | Piece-scoped mechanic: spend one or more resource inventories to produce one or more. |
"
`;
